{
  "abstract": "We resolve the faithful elementary abelian order-9 ($C_3 \\times C_3$) automorphism question for two-colored $(K_5, I_5)$-free graphs across Orders 42, 43, 44, and 45 relevant to $43 \\le R(5,5) \\le 46$. Every faithful $C_3 \\times C_3$ action decomposes into $n_9$ regular 9-orbits, $n_3$ length-3 orbits across the four order-3 stabilizer subgroups, and $n_1$ fixed vertices, yielding 178 faithful orbit-size triples. First, on the induced subgraph $Q_0 \\sqcup X \\sqcup F$ of a single regular 9-orbit plus all short orbits and fixed vertices, combining coset-saturation slope capacities and `design_synthesist`'s three-unit-row exclusion with cross-slope clique, rectangle, opposite-color block, and fixed-clique laws proves $n_3 \\le 8, n_1 \\le 8$ by hand ($N \\le 41$ at $n_9 = 1$) and $n_3 \\le 7, 3n_3 + n_1 \\le 23$ via finite enumeration over the local inequalities, excluding all 49 triples at $n_9 = 1$ ($N \\le 32$) and all 37 triples at $n_9 = 2$ ($N \\le 41$) and reducing $n_9 = 3$ (25 triples) to $n_3 \\ge 5$ or ($n_3 \\in \\{3,4\\}, n_1 \\ge 3$). Second, for $n_9 = 0$ (53 triples), extending `ramsey_5_5_12` Lemma 2 to Order 42 forces two 7-triple classes, refuted by a six-triple hand proof and 20-class in-memory RUP verification. Third, for $n_9 \\in \\{3,4,5\\}$, canonical reductions and in-memory RUP refutations close all remaining cases. Combined with `ramsey_5_5_13` ($C_9$), $9 \\nmid |\\operatorname{Aut}(G)|$ across Orders 42 to 45. This constrains candidate symmetries while leaving $43 \\le R(5,5) \\le 46$ unchanged.",
